experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0010/committee1/systems_reviewer.out:3:  {system: "ACON", url: "https://github.com/microsoft/acon / https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.00615", overlap: "High: long-horizon LLM agent context compression of observations/history, evaluated on AppWorld/OfficeBench/Multi-objective QA; reports 26-54% peak-token reduction and task-success gains. Does not appear to use this packet's exact extractive future-reference predictor/oracle-gap framing."},
experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0010/committee1/systems_reviewer.out:5:  {system: "H2O", url: "https://github.com/FMInference/H2O", overlap: "Medium: attention-heavy-hitter KV eviction retaining recent + high-attention tokens; overlaps with attention-based retention, not agent transcript/tool-result extraction."},
experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0010/committee1/systems_reviewer.out:6:  {system: "SnapKV", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.14469", overlap: "Medium: KV compression by selecting important positions from attention features; reports 3.6x generation speed and 8.2x memory efficiency at 16K tokens; not committed tool-result compression."},
experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0010/committee1/systems_reviewer.out:8:  {system: "vLLM Automatic Prefix Caching", url: "https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/design/prefix_caching/", overlap: "Low: shipping KV prefix reuse with LRU block eviction; reduces recompute, does not compress transcript by future utility."},
experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0010/committee1/systems_reviewer.out:9:  {system: "LMCache", url: "https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache", overlap: "Low: shipping KV reuse/offload for reused text across GPU/CPU/disk/S3 and vLLM/SGLang integrations; cache reuse, not extractive content selection."},
experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0010/committee1/systems_reviewer.out:10:  {system: "TensorRT-LLM KV cache reuse", url: "https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/advanced/kv-cache-reuse.html", overlap: "Low: serving-system KV reuse; not tool-output semantic compression."}
experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0010/committee1/systems_reviewer.out:13:SCALE_REALISM: Does not yet hold at realistic workload. Evidence is a deterministic L0 trace simulation with synthetic salience and success=referenced-span availability, not real attention/citation prediction or task accuracy. ACON already demonstrates real agent benchmarks and token reductions, so this packet must show real tool-output sparsity/predictability and matched real-model task accuracy before promotion.
experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0010/committee1/systems_reviewer.out:14:RATIONALE: PROMPT_VERSION v001. The packet gives strong simulated support for the narrow mechanism: EC beats RT in 633/648 cells with CI [+0.275,+0.307], and EO-EC gap is 0 in sparse+high-predictability. That is a useful mechanism result, not mere glue. But the systems claim is not green because the premise is constructed: ref sparsity, predictability, and salience are synthetic, and task success is availability rather than model accuracy. Prior art is crowded and includes ACON, which directly targets long-horizon agent context compression on AppWorld/OfficeBench/Multi-objective QA and reports 26-54% peak-token reduction plus task-success improvements (https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.00615). H2O/SnapKV/StreamingLLM/LLMLingua cover attention/token/KV selection mechanisms with real models, while vLLM/LMCache/TensorRT-LLM cover shipping cache infrastructure. No located shipping system exactly implements "tool-result-specific extractive retention via causal future-reference prediction with oracle-gap accounting", but closest OSS already covers most surrounding systems surface. Required evidence: real attention/citation predictor AUC for future tool-output references, real tool-agent benchmark accuracy at matched budgets, comparison to ACON/LLMLingua/H2O/SnapKV/StreamingLLM-style baselines, and reproducible GPU traces showing latency/memory/token effects.
experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0010/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:23:MANDATE: is this a systems INSIGHT/DESIGN, or mere engineering integration? Search OSS (vLLM/SGLang/
experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0010/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:24:LMCache/FlashInfer/TensorRT-LLM/etc.) for whether existing systems already implement this mechanism.
experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0010/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:54:## This is the first HELD L0 (effect=support). The make-or-break control (oracle vs causal predictor) came back FOR the claim: causal predictor MATCHES the oracle in the sparse+predictable regime (gap CI [0,0]), beats recency-truncation in 633/648 cells (CI [+0.275,+0.307] excludes 0), honest-negative N3 ('needs oracle') REFUTED. Vote HONESTLY and HOSTILELY — this is a green-candidate, so scrutinize hard. If candidate-grade, name SPECIFIC GPU/real-model required_evidence (researcher: real attention/citation signal as the causal predictor + real task accuracy on a tool-agent benchmark + verify sparsity/predictability hold on REAL tool outputs). novelty_killer: context/KV compression is CROWDED (LLMLingua, H2O, SnapKV, StreamingLLM=the RT arm) — live >=2-source sweep OWED; the ONLY distinct angle claimed is (a) tool-result-specific + (b) retention-as-causal-future-reference-prediction with the oracle gap quantified. Isolate our contribution vs the compression mechanism itself.
